        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/trump-s-acknowledgment-of-hezbollah-utterly-humiliating-for-netanyahu",
        "orario": "20:29",
        "timestamp": 1780424947,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump's acknowledgment of Hezbollah 'utterly humiliating' for Netanyahu Middle East Issued on: 02/06/2026 - 20:29 Modified: 02/06/2026 - 20:37 Israel continued to strike southern Lebanon on Tuesday as Iran-backed Hezbollah attacked its troops there despite an apparent Washington-brokered de-escalation deal and a fourth round of US-hosted talks between Lebanon and Israel. FRANCE 24's Jerusalem correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky explains that \"on the Israeli side we have simply no acknowledgment of this deal\", adding that seeing Trump acknowledge Hezbollah \"has been an utter humiliation\" for Benjamin Netanyahu. 'Healthy consensus in Israel' on pursuing Lebanon campaign, expert says 01/06/2026 Middle East 'Most extreme right-wing fringes of Netanyahu govt call for far greater military action in Lebanon' 01/06/2026 Middle East Kuwait intercepts drones, missiles as US and Iran trade fire 01/06/2026 Middle East Is Israel seeking free reign from US in Lebanon? 01/06/2026 Middle East What is Lebanon's Beaufort Castle, and why have Israeli forces captured it? 31/05/2026 Middle East Israel seizes strategic Beaufort Castle in Lebanon, issues new evacuation orders 31/05/2026 Middle East Three months after the strike, Iranian families still mourn Minab's children 31/05/2026 Middle East Israel orders new evacuations in Lebanon and pushes further north 31/05/2026 Middle East Israeli troops push deeper into Lebanon, crossing the Litani river, as talks expected 30/05/2026 Middle East"
